# next-quest vs next-quest-nextjs — Complete Comparison

> Both apps look and behave identically. Under the hood they use completely
> different mental models for how React code is organized, started, and run.

---

## 1. What kind of app each one is

| | `next-quest` | `next-quest-nextjs` |
|---|---|---|
| **Type** | React SPA (Single Page App) | Next.js App Router (full-stack framework) |
| **Build tool** | Vite | Next.js / Turbopack |
| **Entry point** | `src/main.tsx` | `src/app/layout.tsx` |
| **Routing** | `react-router-dom` (JS-only, client) | File-system routes inside `src/app/` |
| **Server** | None — just serves static files | Node.js dev server (can render on server) |
| **Runs at** | `http://localhost:5173` | `http://localhost:3001` |

