## 7. Components — `'use client'` directive

React SPA components run **only in the browser** — always. So they can freely
use hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`), event handlers (`onClick`), browser APIs
(`navigator.clipboard`, `localStorage`), and Redux selectors.

In Next.js, **components can run on the server by default**. The server has no
`window`, no `localStorage`, no Redux store in memory. You must explicitly
label interactive components:

```tsx
"use client";   // ← top of file, tells Next.js: "only run this in the browser"

import { useState } from "react";
import { useAppSelector } from "@/store/hooks";  // Redux — needs browser
```

### Which components got `'use client'` added

| Component | Why |
|---|---|
| `Navbar.tsx` | Uses Redux selector, `usePathname()` |
| `NotificationStack.tsx` | Uses Redux, `useEffect`, `framer-motion` |
| `SyncIndicator.tsx` | Uses Redux selector |
| `SyncEngine.tsx` | Uses Redux, `useEffect`, fetch |
| `CodeBlock.tsx` | Uses `useState` + `navigator.clipboard` |
| `CodeEditor.tsx` | CodeMirror touches the DOM |
| `CodeExercise.tsx` | Uses Redux dispatch + `useState` |
| `QuizExercise.tsx` | Uses Redux + `useState` |
| `FillExercise.tsx` | Uses `useState` |
| All `app/page.tsx` files | Use Redux selectors |

> `LessonContent.tsx` and `SimulatedBrowser.tsx` are **pure** (no hooks, no
> Redux) so they work fine as server components — no directive needed.

### CodeEditor — dynamic import

CodeMirror directly touches the DOM on import. If Next.js tried to render it on
the server, it would crash. Solution: load it lazily, only in the browser:

```tsx
// React SPA — just import it
import CodeMirror from "@uiw/react-codemirror";

// Next.js — dynamic import inside useEffect (runs only client-side)
useEffect(() => {
  Promise.all([
    import("@uiw/react-codemirror"),
    import("@codemirror/theme-one-dark"),
    import("@codemirror/lang-javascript"),
  ]).then(([cm, { oneDark }, { javascript }]) => {
    setCM({ CodeMirror: cm.default, oneDark, javascript });
  });
}, []);

// Show a skeleton while the editor loads
if (!CM) return <div>Loading editor…</div>;
```

