## 10. End-to-end flow comparison

### React SPA — what happens when you visit `/learn/intro-to-nextjs`

```
Browser requests /learn/intro-to-nextjs
         ↓
Server returns index.html + bundle.js  (same files for EVERY URL)
         ↓
Browser runs bundle.js
         ↓
Redux store created (singleton), redux-persist rehydrates from localStorage
         ↓
BrowserRouter reads window.location.pathname
         ↓
Routes matches "/learn/:slug"  →  renders <LessonPage />
         ↓
LessonPage calls useParams() → { slug: "intro-to-nextjs" }
         ↓
findLesson("intro-to-nextjs") → lesson data from curriculum.ts
         ↓
Page renders with lesson content + exercises
```

### Next.js — what happens when you visit `/learn/intro-to-nextjs`

```
Browser requests /learn/intro-to-nextjs
         ↓
Next.js server matches app/learn/[slug]/page.tsx
         ↓
Server renders layout.tsx shell (HTML, body, Navbar)
+ page.tsx is a "use client" component → rendered in browser
         ↓
HTML skeleton sent to browser immediately  ← faster first paint
         ↓
Browser hydrates: Redux store created via makeStore() + useRef
redux-persist rehydrates from localStorage
         ↓
LessonPage receives params as Promise<{ slug: "intro-to-nextjs" }>
React.use(params) unwraps it → { slug: "intro-to-nextjs" }
         ↓
findLesson("intro-to-nextjs") → lesson data from curriculum.ts
         ↓
Page renders with lesson content + exercises
```

