## 11. Summary of every concrete change made

| What | React SPA | Next.js | Why changed |
|---|---|---|---|
| Entry point | `main.tsx` (you write it) | `app/layout.tsx` (framework calls it) | Next.js owns the boot sequence |
| Router | `react-router-dom` | File-system `app/` folder | Next.js has routing built in |
| Route params | `useParams()` hook | `use(params)` prop | Next.js 15+ made params async |
| Navigation | `<Link to>`, `useNavigate` | `<Link href>`, `useRouter` | Different packages |
| Active link | `<NavLink className={fn}>` | `usePathname()` comparison | Next.js has no NavLink |
| Shell component | `Layout.tsx` with `<Outlet>` | `layout.tsx` with `{children}` | Different composition model |
| Page components | `src/pages/*.tsx` | `src/app/*/page.tsx` | File-system routing |
| Redux store | Module singleton | `makeStore()` factory | Prevent server-side data leakage |
| Redux provider | Inline in `main.tsx` | `StoreProvider.tsx` component | Needs to work in React tree |
| Persistence storage | Always `localStorage` | SSR-safe no-op on server | Server has no localStorage |
| CodeMirror | Direct import | Dynamic `import()` in `useEffect` | Server has no DOM |
| Client markers | None needed | `"use client"` on 10 files | Next.js components default to server |
| Fonts | `<link>` in `index.html` | `next/font/google` | Self-hosting, no FOUT |
| Tailwind config | `tailwind.config.ts` | `@theme` block in CSS | Tailwind v4 changed the API |
| CSS entry | `src/index.css` | `src/app/globals.css` | Next.js convention |
| `import` paths | `../features/...` | `@/features/...` | `@/` alias configured by Next.js |
